    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78-a3">

                <pb facs="0241" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg113"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    338.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Arroyo to Mr. Hall</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 15,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to
                    you a copy of decree No. 323, which the general in charge of the Presidency of
                    the Republic, in the exercise of the executive power, issued to-day in the
                    council of ministers.</p>
                <p>It is very gratifying to me to transmit to you this document, in which you will
                    be pleased to notice that, with great justice, it is disposed to communicate a
                    note of thanks to the honorable diplomatic corps accredited in Central America
                    for their friendly and efficient mediation to obtain the restoration of peace
                    between the Republics of Salvador, Nicaragua, Costa Rica, and Guatemala.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ANGEL MA. ARROYO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
